<title>USA: FSA qualifies seven muni issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies seven muni issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said Thursday it qualified for bond insurance the following seven municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Pottsville School District No 61, Ark., $2.085 million contruction bonds.</p>
<p>--Whittemore-Prescott, Mich., $10.2 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Clarksdale Muni School District, Miss., $7.83 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Middletown City School District, N.Y., $34.884 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Oneida County, N.Y., $15.775 million improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Bilma Public Utility District, Texas, $1.5 million unlimited tax bonds.</p>
<p>--Conroe, Texas, $3.5 million certificates of obligation.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
